                                            "date":  "2026-09-22",
                                            "imageUrl":  null,
                                            "summary":  "Santoli documents a months-long sideways consolidation in the S\u0026P 500 sustained entirely by rotation rather than broad participation. Market breadth has deteriorated significantly Ã¢â‚¬â€ on a day the S\u0026P 500 was up 1.5%, NYSE recorded 160 new 52-week lows against only 29 fresh highs. Semiconductor stocks and mega-cap tech platforms had been under pressure from AI-overspending fears but were beginning to recover.",
                                            "take":  "The market Santoli describes is one that looks healthy at the index level and fragile underneath Ã¢â‚¬â€ exactly the environment where passive investors are lulled and stock-pickers find opportunity. The breadth deterioration is a meaningful risk flag: if the mega-cap tech pillar cracks even modestly on a negative earnings surprise, a regulatory event, or a rate spike, there is no broad-based support to absorb the index. Investors should treat the narrow leadership not as a reason for complacency but as a reason to assess concentration risk Ã¢â‚¬â€ either in their own portfolios or in the cap-weighted index funds that overweight the same handful of stocks doing all the work.",
