                                                              "url":  "https://aswathdamodaran.blogspot.com/2026/09/interest-rates-and-stock-prices-old.html",
                                                              "date":  "2026-09-10",
                                                              "imageUrl":  "https://blogger.googleusercontent.com/img/b/R29vZ2xl/AVvXsEgDslAhzkZu_Oq6rigZLlCaVn-tfCOa1vu3ybROAgHuWdrNTjeWjdAqX6_6ZHMIDNlYg6MmxdA-NciCoeOAwGWdq2GoeHsO1qvCXbrDMAMDkl9uJ5b2cR0cMQAqoH-hEAjvSIA1y6Z3kqp31L-8KS0qvM7hdLfxbLCtu17Ke766hvMmqsGR26fCLqJtnaA/s1718/USTreasuryRates2026.jpg",
                                                              "summary":  "Damodaran examines the 2026 rise in U.S. Treasury rates ÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â€šÂ¬Ã¢â‚¬Â the 10-year reaching 4.75% by August ÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â€šÂ¬Ã¢â‚¬Â and challenges the reflexive assumption that higher rates must depress equity values. Using historical data since 1962, he distinguishes between market-set rates and \u0027intrinsic\u0027 rates derived from inflation and GDP growth, finding the current rate environment is within historical norms. Despite rate increases, S\u0026P 500 and NASDAQ rose substantially, driven by 11-plus percent analyst earnings estimate upgrades for 2026 and 2027 that offset the higher discount rate headwind.",
                                                              "take":  "Damodaran\u0027s central insight ÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â€šÂ¬Ã¢â‚¬Â that the rate-to-stock-price relationship is company-specific, not universal ÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â€šÂ¬Ã¢â‚¬Â is the analytically correct frame but is chronically underweighted by market commentators who treat every yield spike as a sell signal. The real stress test for any equity position in a rising-rate environment is not \u0027are rates going up?\u0027 but \u0027is this company\u0027s earnings growth fast enough to outpace the discount rate increase?\u0027 ÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â€šÂ¬Ã¢â‚¬Â a distinction that separates quality compounders from rate-sensitive zombies. For enterprise AI investors specifically, companies whose AI investments are generating measurable cash flow growth (hyperscalers, productivity software) are insulated in ways that AI-adjacent pure-plays with long cash-flow timelines are not. The Fed\u0027s limited influence on long-term rates, per Damodaran\u0027s analysis, also means rate forecasting as an investment input is mostly noise; focus on company fundamentals instead.",
                                                              "isNew":  true
